    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41458" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτρύζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>squeak beside</i> or <i>over,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέμφιγες -τρύζουσι θανόντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Euph.
					134
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τό μοι τελχῖνες -τρύζουσιν</span>”
				<i>mutter,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Aet.Oxy.</u>
					2079
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1.1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῦς -τρύξας τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					112.8
				</span></i>
			 : abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[τέττιξ] ἁβρὸν ἐ.</span>”
				<i>chirps,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					6.54
				</span></i>
			 (Paul. Sil.). (In part perh. 
				f.l.for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τρίζω.</span>
			)</div>
